Filed by langertha-llm-advisor, 2026-09-01. Anthropic docs read 2026-09-01 (note:
docs.claude.com / docs.anthropic.com now 301/302-redirect to platform.claude.com).

ADR 0005 decision 2 says: "When a caller asks for response_format on an engine with no native
response_format but native forced tools (Anthropic), the engine synthesizes a tool from the
schema, forces tool_choice to it, and chat_response lifts the resulting tool_use input back into
Response.content." That premise is now false in BOTH halves.

## 1. Anthropic HAS native structured output, GA, no beta header

https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/structured-outputs (read 2026-09-01).
The parameter is **output_config.format** -- not response_format, and no longer output_format:

    "output_config": { "format": { "type": "json_schema", "schema": { ... } } }

Verbatim: "The `output_format` parameter has moved to `output_config.format`, and beta headers are
no longer required. The API continues to accept the old beta header
(`structured-outputs-2025-11-13`) and the `output_format` request field for a transition period".
Changelog 2026-01-29: out of beta for Sonnet 4.5 / Opus 4.5 / Haiku 4.5.

Supported models: claude-fable-5-1, claude-mythos-5-1, claude-fable-5, claude-mythos-5,
claude-mythos-preview, claude-opus-5, claude-opus-4-8, claude-opus-4-7, claude-opus-4-6,
claude-sonnet-5, claude-sonnet-4-6, claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929, claude-opus-4-5-20251101,
claude-haiku-4-5-20251001.

Also new and relevant: **strict tool use** is GA, no beta header --
`"strict": true` as a top-level property of a tool definition (alongside name / description /
input_schema), requiring `additionalProperties: false` + `required`. Guarantees "Tool `input`
strictly follows the `input_schema`" and "Tool `name` is always valid".
https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/strict-tool-use
`Langertha::Tool->to_anthropic` does not emit it.

## 2. The workaround now 400s on Anthropic's newest models

https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/tool-reference and the errors page.
`tool_choice` type `any` and type `tool` are REJECTED with HTTP 400 in two situations:

  - **Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1** -- "`any` and `tool` return a 400 error"
    (changelog 2026-09-01). Server message: `tool_choice: type "tool" and "any" are not
    supported for this model.` Enforced on count_tokens and Batches too.
  - Manual extended thinking (`thinking: {type:"enabled"}`) -- "`any` and `tool` are not
    supported and result in an error".

`Role::AnthropicCompatible::_translate_response_format` synthesizes a tool and forces
`tool_choice` onto it. On claude-fable-5-1 / claude-mythos-5-1 that is a guaranteed 400 for ANY
caller who sets `response_format` -- the very thing the rewrite exists to make work. Anthropic's
own documented fallback for those models is `auto` + a prompt instruction, `strict: true`, or
structured outputs, i.e. exactly the native path in point 1.

This is also the sharpest instance yet of the model-gated-capability gap (ADR 0002): the flag
`tool_choice_named` is engine-wide and true for every AnthropicBase engine, while the wire truth
is per model. `supports('tool_choice_named')` cannot express "true on sonnet-5, 400 on fable-5-1".

## 3. Design constraint for whoever implements the native path: output_config is SHARED

`Langertha::Reasoning::to_anthropic` already returns `output_config => { effort => $e }`
(Reasoning.pm:227-239). Native structured output needs `output_config => { format => {...} }`.
Both land in the same flat kwargs list that `chat_request` spreads into the body, so a naive
second `output_config => ...` OVERWRITES the first and silently drops the effort (or the format).
The two must be MERGED into one `output_config` hash. That is a new kind of collision for the
ADR 0009 quartet -- until now each concern owned a disjoint body key. Worth an ADR note.

## Suggested direction (needs a maintainer decision, not a blind edit)

1. Add `response_format_json_schema` as a NATIVE Anthropic capability, emitted as
   `output_config.format`, merged with any `output_config.effort` from `Reasoning`.
2. Keep the synthetic-tool rewrite as the fallback for the models that predate native structured
   output, gated on the model id -- OR drop it entirely if the supported-model list above covers
   everything Langertha targets (it covers every non-retired Claude model).
3. Amend ADR 0005: direction 2 becomes "historical, superseded by native output_config.format"
   while direction 1 (Perplexity: forced tool -> response_format) stays live.
4. Either way, `tool_choice` type `tool`/`any` must not be emitted for
   claude-fable-5-1 / claude-mythos-5-1. That needs a model-gated correction; the existing
   precedent is `Engine::OpenAI::_max_tokens_key` (a per-model regex inside the engine) and
   `Langertha::Reasoning::_is_fable_class` / `to_gemini_level` (per-model clamps inside the value
   object). A third instance of the same unnamed pattern -- see the concept red-team note.

